\\ A try whose quotation consumes a stack argument compiles under `--interpreter-fallback=false`
\\ instead of failing the NC.13 abstract-stack underflow.
\\
\\ This is the static-file-handler shape: the quot consumes `path`, and an `if` arm reaches below
\\ the result via `swap` for a value kept from before the try.
\\
\\ `try`'s row-variable effect resolves the real arity from the quotation literal per call site,
\\ so the word's own body compiles concretely rather than underflowing.
demo: ( n path -- s ) [
  [ 100 swap / ] try
  dup result:ok?
  [ unwrap-or-throw swap + >string ]
  [ drop drop "error" ]
  if
] ;

5 4 demo print-line
5 0 demo print-line

\\ A try whose quotation consumes two arguments, confirming arity resolves for
\\ counts other than one.
add-safely: ( a b -- s ) [
  [ + ] try
  dup result:ok? [ unwrap-or-throw >string ] [ drop "err" ] if
] ;

10 20 add-safely print-line
